# Keeps the build context small. The build stage does `COPY . .`, so anything
# left in here is tarred, hashed and written into an image layer on every
# `./build.sh` -- without this file that is ~6GB, almost none of which the
# build reads. Podman reads .containerignore; Docker falls back to
# .dockerignore, which is a symlink to this.

# The retail disc and everything extracted from it. build.sh mounts rom/ in at
# run time precisely so it stays out of the image.
rom/

# The split. 70MB of the context, mounted in by build.sh for the same reason
# rom/ is: it is generated, it has to survive between runs, and a re-split has
# to land in the tree rather than in a copy that goes away with the container.
asm/

# A checkout of the private repository: retail binaries. What the build needs
# of it is copied into rom/, which is mounted.
.private/

# Reverse-engineering scratch: the IDA database and the CodeWarrior installs
# the compiler under tools/compilers was lifted from. Half a gig, unused by
# the build.
re/

# decomp-permuter, a development tool the build never invokes.
permuting/

# Generated. Copying build/ in is not just wasteful but wrong: its
# CMakeCache.txt records whichever source path last configured it (a host
# path, or /workspaces/dcdecomp from the devcontainer), which makes the
# configure inside the container fail or reuse stale paths.
build/
ref/
**/__pycache__/
ctx.c

# History is not needed to compile.
.git/

# Editor and agent configuration.
.vscode/
.devcontainer/
.claude/
.codex/
.agents/

# The lock every build of the tree takes; see scripts/build/cmake.sh.
.build.lock
